mapping "W379.1" source="W379" target="218069008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W379 SNOMED CT 218069008 = ICD-10 W37 (Explosion and rupture of pressurized tire, pipe or
        hose), place unspecified (Swedish extension adds place/activity detail to the 3-char base W37).
        Target (Athena 437740) =, standard (S, valid 2002-01-31 to 2099-12-31). Base ICD-10 W37
        Athena-crosswalks to 437740. Target legitimately subsumes the source: tyre/pipe/hose explosions
        are a subtype of pressure-vessel explosions. The deprecated [X] SNOMED CT 220755001
        (Explosion.tire/pipe/hose, occurrence at unspecified place) is the literal ICD-10 crosswalk but
        is non-standard (invalid_reason=D in OMOP); the standard 218069008 is preferred. high: verified
        crosswalk, one-level broader.
        """
}
mapping "W3790.1" source="W3790" target="218069008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W3790 = W37 (tyre/pipe/hose pressurized explosion), place unspecified, during
        sport/exercise (Swedish activity subcode of W379). Target SNOMED CT 218069008 (Athena 437740) =,
        standard (S). SNOMED CT has no concept combining pressure-vessel explosion + activity dimension;
        the activity qualifier (sport) has no standard representation. Broader: target subsumes the
        device/cause axis but drops the activity axis. moderate: best available standard concept,
        dimension mismatch on activity.
        """
}
mapping "W3791.1" source="W3791" target="218069008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
